     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, so you can't verify a clinical order. The prescriber needs to review the order and either enter it themselves or confirm it to me directly.\n\nIf the intended dose was 5 mg or 10 mg once daily by mouth, a clinician can confirm that and I'll enter it. If a prescriber really does intend a dose above the labeled maximum, for example in a monitored setting, they should enter it themselves through the hospital's normal process. That process includes pharmacist review and a documented rationale.\n\nIf you tell me who the prescriber is, I can help you get the request to them."
      }
     ],
